      "rev_n_1_56bddf_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_56bddf_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_56bddf",
        "thought_text": "Compare the sorted versions of s and t. If the sorted s is lexicographically less than the sorted t, then it's always possible to rearrange s to be less than t.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1791446274.135361
      },
      "rev_n_2_74eb57_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_74eb57_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_74eb57",
        "thought_text": "Check if there exists any character in s that is lexicographically less than the smallest character in t. If so, rearrange s to start with this character, ensuring s' < t'.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1791446274.135384
      },
      "rev_n_3_0ff40c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_0ff40c_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_0ff40c",
        "thought_text": "If the lengths of s and t are the same and every character in s is greater than or equal to the corresponding character in t when both are sorted, then it's impossible to make s' < t'. Otherwise, it's possible.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1791446274.135392
      },
      "rev_n_1_56bddf_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_56bddf_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_56bddf",
        "thought_text": "The issue arises because sorting both strings and comparing them directly does not account for all possible rearrangements that could make s' < t'. Instead, we should consider the frequency of each character in both strings and determine if there exists a way to rearrange them such that s' < t' lexicographically.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_56bddf_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_44385b3fa2",
        "created_at": 1791446287.3528771
      },
      "rev_n_1_56bddf_2": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_56bddf_2",
        "node_id": "n_1_56bddf",
        "thought_text": "The current approach incorrectly assumes that if any character in `s` has a lower frequency than the corresponding character in `t`, then `s'` can be made lexicographically smaller than `t'`. This logic fails when the characters with differing frequencies do not appear in the same position in the lexicographical order. A correct approach should consider the cumulative frequency of characters up to each position in the alphabet to determine if `s'` can be made lexicographically smaller than `t'`.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_56bddf_1",
        "feedback_id": "fb_9643bd0b24",
        "created_at": 1791446308.859375
      }
    }
